# Test fixtures encode byte-level defects on purpose: BOMs, CRLF, mixed
# line endings, invisible Cf characters. git's core.autocrlf is `true` on
# this machine, which rewrites line endings on add and checkout -- and it
# already destroyed two fixtures in commit ddc5089: mixed_endings.md was
# stored with zero CRLF, so the "mixed" defect it exists to reproduce was
# gone from the repository while verify.py still passed against the
# working tree.
#
# That is exactly the failure this repository studies: a check that stays
# green while the thing it checks has been silently normalised away.
#
# -text disables all end-of-line conversion. Do not remove it.
tests/fixtures/** -text

# Everything else: normalise to LF in the repository, regardless of the
# local autocrlf setting, so diffs stay readable across machines.
*.md   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.xml  text eol=lf

# ...except the fixture tree, re-stated after the globs above so it wins.
tests/fixtures/** -text
